    "rules": {
      "amplitude": "quantiles (inclusive) of non-zero period values; CV2 = (population sd / mean)^2 of non-zero values",
      "auto": "auto = every granularity at or coarser than the timestamps' resolution (hour needs a time of day) with 2..100,000 periods in span",
      "by": "by: the top N groups by row count (default 5, ties by value); other groups and rows with a missing key are counted, not analysed; each group's span runs from its own first to its own last timestamp",
      "cycle": "present when a dominant ACF lag >= 2 (supported local peak above the per-lag band) also exceeds the family-wise band",
      "duration": "run lengths in periods of consecutive zero and consecutive non-zero periods; a missing period ends a run",
      "frequency": "zero share = zero periods / observed periods; inter-event interval = periods from one non-zero period to the next with no missing period between them (mean is the ADI alias); intervals that span a missing period are counted separately and excluded",
      "missingness": "valid pairs are counted per lag; a lag with fewer than max(10, n/4) valid pairs is not estimable (distinct from an estimate near 0) and never counts toward present or absent; with missing periods the bands use the per-lag valid pair count, n_k = pairs at lag k (complete series: n_k = n); PACF stops at the first non-estimable lag; supported = estimable and lag <= n/4",
      "observation": "value series: a period with no row (or only rows without a parsed value) is a missing observation, a period whose values sum to 0 is a zero; event series: a period with no row has no recorded event (0 counted), and the table cannot say whether the process was observed then",
      "regularise": "periods run from the floor of the first to the floor of the last parsed timestamp; value series sum parsed values per period, event series count rows per period; week = ISO week starting Monday",
      "reliability": "n < 30 observed periods: insufficient (applies to every signal, including zero periods and bursts); zero variance: undefined; lag > n/4: poorly supported",
      "signal": "present when |r_k| exceeds the family-wise band z(1-0.025/L)/sqrt(n_k) at any supported lag (Bonferroni over the L supported lags of this one correlogram; not adjusted across granularities, groups or values vs occurrence); absent = not detected under this rule, not evidence of absence; insufficient evidence under the reliability rule",
      "spectral": "periodogram peak (scipy.signal.periodogram, mean removed) on gap-free series only; requires the stats extra",
      "wavelength": "ACF r_k = sum over pairs observed at t and t+k of (x_t-m)(x_t+k-m) / sum over observed (x_t-m)^2; PACF by Durbin-Levinson; per-lag 95% band +/-1.96/sqrt(n); dominant lag = supported local ACF peak above the band"
